{"base_rate":0.47761194029850745,"brier":0.15642265943012212,"bss":0.3730523944805194,"bss_hi":0.45804837049801467,"bss_lo":0.2760759221640749,"chart":{"base":[474.9,143.0],"fp":[387.2,248.8],"lead":"62,267.5 272,251.3 482,201.2 692,130.4","note":{"base":"skill 0.37 — higher than 72% of cities","fp":"low end +11pp, high end +12pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.0 °C — better than 77% of cities","rel":"promised 3% → rained 14%; promised 94% → rained 83%"},"rel":"83.3,404.7 359.3,284.1 657.1,105.5"},"country":"NL","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.09890094979647221,"ess":327.48555308599737,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Groningen</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Groningen rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>88%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>9%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 737 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nGRONINGEN-1, 4.6 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.37, ranked 61 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(33&ndash;114) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>9%</b></td><td class='num'>221</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>13%</td><td class='num'><b>31%</b></td><td class='num'>68</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>33%</td><td class='num'><b>34%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>61%</td><td class='num'><b>50%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>82%</td><td class='num'><b>69%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>88%</b></td><td class='num'>221</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Groningen</b> <span class=\"muted\">Netherlands</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;48% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 48% of days.</p><p>The forecast did clearly better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.37</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>33&ndash;114\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>737 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Groningen &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Groningen\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"59.76199095022624,377.05882352941177 103.18705882352941,306.92500000000075 175.9844736842105,223.94736842105263 274.17289473684207,118.57894736842104 349.31840000000005,51.97333333333336 406.98633484162895,18.0 406.98633484162895,29.529411764705856 349.31840000000005,115.06666666666666 274.17289473684207,200.0 175.9844736842105,300.57894736842104 103.18705882352941,360.5882352941176 59.76199095022624,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"208.1492537313433\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"208.1492537313433\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"59.76199095022624,349.05882352941177 103.18705882352941,269.5882352941176 175.9844736842105,257.4736842105263 274.17289473684207,200.0 349.31840000000005,129.62666666666667 406.98633484162895,60.823529411764696\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 9% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 221 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"59.76199095022624\" cy=\"349.05882352941177\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 13%&amp;#10;It rained 31% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 68 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"103.18705882352941\" cy=\"269.5882352941176\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 33%&amp;#10;It rained 34% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"175.9844736842105\" cy=\"257.4736842105263\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 61%&amp;#10;It rained 50% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"274.17289473684207\" cy=\"200.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 82%&amp;#10;It rained 69% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 75 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"349.31840000000005\" cy=\"129.62666666666667\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 88% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 221 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"406.98633484162895\" cy=\"60.823529411764696\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(48%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Groningen the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.48) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (0.25).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>54%</td><td class='num'>0.251</td><td class='num'>12.7%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>46%</td><td class='num'>0.284</td><td class='num'>13.3%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>61%</td><td class='num'>0.356</td><td class='num'>10.0%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>198</td><td class='num'>32%</td><td class='num'>0.483</td><td class='num'>5.5%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":53.21917,"lon":6.56667,"n":737,"n_cities":216,"name":"Groningen","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.0580000000000004,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.00497737556561086,"n":221,"obs":0.09049773755656108,"sig":true},{"hi":0.24,"lo":0.0580000000000004,"mean":0.12764705882352942,"n":68,"obs":0.3088235294117647,"sig":true},{"hi":0.47,"lo":0.24,"mean":0.33328947368421047,"n":76,"obs":0.34210526315789475,"sig":false},{"hi":0.74,"lo":0.47,"mean":0.6106578947368421,"n":76,"obs":0.5,"sig":false},{"hi":0.8920000000000005,"lo":0.74,"mean":0.8229333333333334,"n":75,"obs":0.6933333333333334,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.8920000000000005,"mean":0.9858371040723982,"n":221,"obs":0.8823529411764706,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":4.6,"provisional":false,"rank":61,"rank_hi":114.02499999999998,"rank_lo":33.0,"reliability":0.011412975900122248,"resolution":0.10336871043223067,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"groningen","station":"GRONINGEN-1","timezone":"Europe/Amsterdam"}